Z||000007||3FastbackGTs||02-07-2001||10:29 PM||||UMMMMMMMMMMM....WTF!...DUDE!  What are you doing? why dismantle your car to paint it with spray cans only to have it painted again? And further more if you were going thru the process of taking you car apart for a paint job...( I'm still scratching my head over that one) even for a color change...why didn't you just take all your little peices down to the guy you are going to have clear coat your "almost professional" spray can paint joband just have him put a "completely professional" paint job on em'? I paint cars and last time I bought paint for all the Fieros I have painted.. it was approx. $130 for all the paint reducers and clear coat.<BR>How many cans of spray paint did you go thru doing this and at what cost for an "almost professional" (not) paint job? I'm sure your intentions were noble..I have color change many Fieros without removing all the body panels and you would be hard pressed to find any signs if it ever being another color.oh and next time if you choose to paint "almost professionally"<BR>I would unplug that Toaster you got cookin' in the background or we might be reading your next post after you get out of a professional Burn unit at the hospital. just some friendly advice. just curious..did you use Testors, Krylon or Rustoleum? ||||reg||11
