Z||000009||MooCow||02-07-2001||10:50 PM||||All I am doing is painting the edges with the spray can.  In the picture all that yellow you see is covered by the ground FX.  I took the ground FX off to paint underneath it.  I am not painting the whole car with spray cans, I'm not that dumb.  It would cost a lot of money to do it in spray cans and would turn out crappy. So far like you said  it has been around $130, but a little more cause for 2 quarts costed me over $100. The reason I took all the body panels off was because Ed Parks told me that to paint a Fiero a new color you must remove the body panels to get the edges.  Then put it back together and get it painted and clear coated.<BR>Thats why in the picture you still see red cause that is the part that the proffesional is doing.  I was also told not to paint all the body panels while off the car or the color could miss match by spraying one darker or lighter than the other.<BR>I'm not trying to sound like a jacka$$ or anything and I do respect the fact that you gave me your input.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||8
